Thx,<br><br>I searched the forum the best I could, but it is not clear to me yet how to get a "aprs message" added to the aprs beacon sent to a sat. Same as sent to terrestial aprs stations and know in opengd77 CPS aprs setting &lt;comment&gt;<br><br>e.g. This is the original line in satellite.txt:<br>25544U,ISS     ,437.800,145.990,     67,       0,145.825,145.825,145.800,      0,RS0ISS<br><br>Can I add my " aprs message" &lt;Hello World&gt; just like this:<br>25544U,ISS     ,437.800,145.990,     67,       0,145.825,145.825,145.800,      0,RS0ISS Hello World<br><br>Or should I use a comma or whatever .....?<br><br>I will try the above example. Was just wondering what the protocol is.<br><br>Thx and 73's<br>pd2ch<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8499">PD2CH</a> — Fri May 30, 2025 8:25 am</p><hr />
